=== systemctl ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Query or send control commands to the system manager.


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  systemctl [OPTIONS...] COMMAND ...


POSITIONALS (1) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  COMMAND


FLAGS (56) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-h, --help               Show this help
    --version            Show package version
    --system             Connect to system manager
    --user               Connect to user service manager
-H, --host [USER@]HOST   Operate on remote host
-M, --machine CONTAINER  Operate on a local container
-t, --type TYPE          List units of a particular type
    --state STATE        List units with particular LOAD or SUB or ACTIVE
                         state
    --failed             Shortcut for --state=failed
-p, --property NAME      Show only properties by this name
-P NAME                  Equivalent to --value --property=NAME
-a, --all                Show all properties/all units currently in memory,
                         including dead/empty ones. To list all units
                         installed on the system, use 'list-unit-files'
                         instead.
-l, --full               Don't ellipsize unit names on output
-r, --recursive          Show unit list of host and local containers
    --reverse            Show reverse dependencies with 'list-dependencies'
    --with-dependencies  Show unit dependencies with 'status', 'cat',
                         'list-units', and 'list-unit-files'.
    --job-mode MODE      Specify how to deal with already queued jobs, when
                         queueing a new job
-T, --show-transaction   When enqueuing a unit job, show full transaction
    --show-types         When showing sockets, explicitly show their type
    --value              When showing properties, only print the value
    --check-inhibitors MODE Whether to check inhibitors before shutting
                         down, sleeping, or hibernating
-i                       Shortcut for --check-inhibitors=no
    --kill-whom WHOM     Whom to send signal to
    --kill-value INT     Signal value to enqueue
-s, --signal SIGNAL      Which signal to send
    --what RESOURCES     Which types of resources to remove
    --now                Start or stop unit after enabling or disabling it
    --dry-run            Only print what would be done Currently supported
                         by verbs: halt, poweroff, reboot, kexec,
                         soft-reboot, suspend, hibernate,
                         suspend-then-hibernate, hybrid-sleep, default,
                         rescue, emergency, and exit.
-q, --quiet              Suppress output
    --no-warn            Suppress several warnings shown by default
    --wait               For (re)start, wait until service stopped again For
                         is-system-running, wait until startup is completed
    --no-block           Do not wait until operation finished
    --no-wall            Don't send wall message before
                         halt/power-off/reboot
    --no-reload          Don't reload daemon after en-/dis-abling unit files
    --legend BOOL        Enable/disable the legend (column headers and
                         hints)
    --no-pager           Do not pipe output into a pager
    --no-ask-password    Do not ask for system passwords
    --global             Edit/enable/disable/mask default user unit files
                         globally
    --runtime            Edit/enable/disable/mask unit files temporarily
                         until next reboot
-f, --force              When enabling unit files, override existing
                         symlinks When shutting down, execute action
                         immediately
    --preset-mode        Apply only enable, only disable, or all presets
    --root PATH          Edit/enable/disable/mask unit files in the
                         specified root directory
    --image PATH         Edit/enable/disable/mask unit files in the
                         specified disk image
    --image-policy POLICY Specify disk image dissection policy
-n, --lines INTEGER      Number of journal entries to show
-o, --output STRING      Change journal output mode (short, short-precise,
                         short-iso, short-iso-precise, short-full,
                         short-monotonic, short-unix, short-delta, verbose,
                         export, json, json-pretty, json-sse, cat)
    --firmware-setup     Tell the firmware to show the setup menu on next
                         boot
    --boot-loader-menu TIME Boot into boot loader menu on next boot
    --boot-loader-entry NAME Boot into a specific boot loader entry on next
                         boot
    --plain              Print unit dependencies as a list instead of a tree
    --timestamp FORMAT   Change format of printed timestamps (pretty, unix,
                         us, utc, us+utc)
    --read-only          Create read-only bind mount
    --mkdir              Create directory before mounting, if missing
    --marked             Restart/reload previously marked units
    --drop-in NAME       Edit unit files using the specified drop-in file
                         name
    --when TIME          Schedule halt/power-off/reboot/kexec action after a
                         certain timestamp

=== systemctl list-units ===
List units currently in memory


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  list-units [PATTERN...]

=== systemctl list-automounts ===
List automount units currently in memory, ordered by path


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  list-automounts [PATTERN...]

=== systemctl list-paths ===
List path units currently in memory, ordered by path


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  list-paths [PATTERN...]

=== systemctl list-sockets ===
List socket units currently in memory, ordered by address


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  list-sockets [PATTERN...]

=== systemctl list-timers ===
List timer units currently in memory, ordered by next elapse


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  list-timers [PATTERN...]

=== systemctl is-active ===
Check whether units are active


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  is-active PATTERN...

=== systemctl is-failed ===
Check whether units are failed or system is in degraded state


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  is-failed [PATTERN...]

=== systemctl status ===
Show runtime status of one or more units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  status [PATTERN...|PID...]

=== systemctl show ===
Show properties of one or more units/jobs or the manager


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  show [PATTERN...|JOB...]

=== systemctl cat ===
Show files and drop-ins of specified units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  cat PATTERN...

=== systemctl help ===
Show manual for one or more units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  help PATTERN...|PID...

=== systemctl list-dependencies ===
Recursively show units which are required or wanted by the units or by which
those units are required or wanted


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  list-dependencies [UNIT...]

=== systemctl start ===
Start (activate) one or more units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  start UNIT...

=== systemctl stop ===
Stop (deactivate) one or more units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  stop UNIT...

=== systemctl reload ===
Reload one or more units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  reload UNIT...

=== systemctl restart ===
Start or restart one or more units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  restart UNIT...

=== systemctl try-restart ===
Restart one or more units if active


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  try-restart UNIT...

=== systemctl reload-or-restart ===
Reload one or more units if possible, otherwise start or restart


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  reload-or-restart UNIT...

=== systemctl try-reload-or-restart ===
If active, reload one or more units, if supported, otherwise restart


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  try-reload-or-restart UNIT...

=== systemctl isolate ===
Start one unit and stop all others


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  isolate UNIT

=== systemctl kill ===
Send signal to processes of a unit


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  kill UNIT...

=== systemctl clean ===
Clean runtime, cache, state, logs or configuration of unit


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  clean UNIT...

=== systemctl freeze ===
Freeze execution of unit processes


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  freeze PATTERN...

=== systemctl thaw ===
Resume execution of a frozen unit


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  thaw PATTERN...

=== systemctl set-property ===
Sets one or more properties of a unit


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  set-property UNIT PROPERTY=VALUE...

=== systemctl bind ===
Bind-mount a path from the host into a unit's namespace


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  bind UNIT PATH [PATH]

=== systemctl mount-image ===
Mount an image from the host into a unit's namespace


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  mount-image UNIT PATH [PATH [OPTS]]

=== systemctl service-log-level ===
Get/set logging threshold for service


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  service-log-level SERVICE [LEVEL]

=== systemctl service-log-target ===
Get/set logging target for service


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  service-log-target SERVICE [TARGET]

=== systemctl reset-failed ===
Reset failed state for all, one, or more units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  reset-failed [PATTERN...]

=== systemctl whoami ===
Return unit caller or specified PIDs are part of


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  whoami [PID...]

=== systemctl list-unit-files ===
List installed unit files


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  list-unit-files [PATTERN...]

=== systemctl enable ===
Enable one or more unit files


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  enable [UNIT...|PATH...]

=== systemctl disable ===
Disable one or more unit files


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  disable UNIT...

=== systemctl reenable ===
Reenable one or more unit files


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  reenable UNIT...

=== systemctl preset ===
Enable/disable one or more unit files based on preset configuration


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  preset UNIT...

=== systemctl preset-all ===
Enable/disable all unit files based on preset configuration

=== systemctl is-enabled ===
Check whether unit files are enabled


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  is-enabled UNIT...

=== systemctl mask ===
Mask one or more units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  mask UNIT...

=== systemctl unmask ===
Unmask one or more units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  unmask UNIT...

=== systemctl link ===
Link one or more units files into the search path


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  link PATH...

=== systemctl revert ===
Revert one or more unit files to vendor version


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  revert UNIT...

=== systemctl add-wants ===
Add 'Wants' dependency for the target on specified one or more units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  add-wants TARGET UNIT...

=== systemctl add-requires ===
Add 'Requires' dependency for the target on specified one or more units


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  add-requires TARGET UNIT...

=== systemctl edit ===
Edit one or more unit files


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  edit UNIT...

=== systemctl get-default ===
Get the name of the default target

=== systemctl set-default ===
Set the default target


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  set-default TARGET

=== systemctl list-machines ===
List local containers and host


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  list-machines [PATTERN...]

=== systemctl list-jobs ===
List jobs


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  list-jobs [PATTERN...]

=== systemctl cancel ===
Cancel all, one, or more jobs


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  cancel [JOB...]

=== systemctl show-environment ===
Dump environment

=== systemctl set-environment ===
Set one or more environment variables


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  set-environment VARIABLE=VALUE...

=== systemctl unset-environment ===
Unset one or more environment variables


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  unset-environment VARIABLE...

=== systemctl import-environment ===
Import all or some environment variables


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  import-environment VARIABLE...

=== systemctl daemon-reload ===
Reload systemd manager configuration

=== systemctl daemon-reexec ===
Reexecute systemd manager

=== systemctl log-level ===
Get/set logging threshold for manager


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  log-level [LEVEL]

=== systemctl log-target ===
Get/set logging target for manager


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  log-target [TARGET]

=== systemctl service-watchdogs ===
Get/set service watchdog state


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  service-watchdogs [BOOL]

=== systemctl is-system-running ===
Check whether system is fully running

=== systemctl default ===
Enter system default mode

=== systemctl rescue ===
Enter system rescue mode

=== systemctl emergency ===
Enter system emergency mode

=== systemctl halt ===
Shut down and halt the system

=== systemctl poweroff ===
Shut down and power-off the system

=== systemctl reboot ===
Shut down and reboot the system

=== systemctl kexec ===
Shut down and reboot the system with kexec

=== systemctl soft-reboot ===
Shut down and reboot userspace

=== systemctl exit ===
Request user instance or container exit


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  exit [EXIT_CODE]

=== systemctl switch-root ===
Change to a different root file system


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  switch-root [ROOT [INIT]]

=== systemctl suspend ===
Suspend the system

=== systemctl hibernate ===
Hibernate the system

=== systemctl hybrid-sleep ===
Hibernate and suspend the system

=== systemctl suspend-then-hibernate ===
Suspend the system, wake after a period of time, and hibernate
